tdesktop's codegen now emits a per-translation-unit subset of lang keys instead of
one header with all of them (desktop-app/codegen "Added subsets of lang keys for
each translation unit"). The scanner that decides which keys a .cpp needs matches
the hardcoded `lng_` prefix, so AyuGram's own `ayu_*` keys never make it into any
subset and every `tr::ayu_*` fails with "is not a member of 'tr'".

Only bites the Ninja/Makefile generators - generate_lang.cmake skips subsets
entirely for Visual Studio/Xcode, which is why upstream CI stays green.

--- a/Telegram/codegen/codegen/lang/subsets.cpp
+++ b/Telegram/codegen/codegen/lang/subsets.cpp
@@ -191,13 +191,12 @@
 
 void Scan(const QByteArray &content, Scanned &result) {
 	const auto data = content.constData();
 	const auto size = content.size();
 	for (auto i = qsizetype(0); i + 4 < size; ++i) {
-		if (data[i] != 'l'
-			|| data[i + 1] != 'n'
-			|| data[i + 2] != 'g'
+		if ((!(data[i] == 'l' && data[i + 1] == 'n' && data[i + 2] == 'g')
+			&& !(data[i] == 'a' && data[i + 1] == 'y' && data[i + 2] == 'u'))
 			|| data[i + 3] != '_'
 			|| (i > 0 && IsIdentifierChar(data[i - 1]))) {
 			continue;
 		}
 		auto till = i + 4;
